Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 10:09:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/25] Modeling Algorithms - Rebuild fillet pieces that break
 the tangency of the trace

On the FreeCAD screw of the previous commits, the fillet of the start wall
next to the fillet of the root (both of radius 1) left a loop on the wall
or failed: the walking keeps the center of the ball in the section plane,
and near the root the surfdata after the one on the fillet of the root
starts with a hook (radii 0.8-1), or, when the ball does not fit into the
root (above 1), the walking makes a swallowtail there. At radius 1 and
above the surfdata on the root is also twisted, and the filling crashed on
a neighbor computed out of its face.

PerformSetOfKGen now rebuilds such a surfdata with the filling it uses for
a twisted one:
- a surfdata is also rebuilt when the trace on one of its sides breaks the
  tangency with the trace of a neighbor on the same face, or a neighbor
  starts or ends with a sharp turn (more than 10 degrees between chords of
  1/100 of its trace, on its first or last 40 percent), the other side
  going on smoothly (one face or smooth edges) and the stripe not
  periodic;
- the bad end of such a neighbor (twisted or not) is left to the filling:
  its trace starts (ends) after it;
- when the neighbors turn the same way as the chord between them, the
  rebuilt trace is a cubic tangent to them, with the tangents of a
  circular arc turning by the same angle;
- otherwise the ball does not fit: the trace before is cut where the trace
  after, extended back straight, meets it (CornerOnPrevious), or at their
  crossing, and the trace of the rebuilt surfdata on that face is the
  straight segment from that corner, or nothing when both traces start
  there (the filling ends in a point);
- the compatibility at the corners of these fillings is checked, which
  keeps their tangency to the faces and to the neighbors within 0.3
  degree instead of 2 (up to 5 degrees next to the corner for radii
  1.38-1.42, where the segment is very short);
- the filling is oriented as the surfdata before it;
- a twisted surfdata whose neighbor on the twisted side is computed out
  of its face fails as one without neighbor instead of crashing.

The fillet of the wall is valid for radii 0.08-1.82 (except 0.44-0.46 and
0.525, where the walking fails as before), its trace tangent to the wall;
the full chain of the file with FreeCAD's refine (with the next commit)
stays valid with tolerance 2.4e-4.

Draw tests bugs/modalg_8/fillet_wall_profile_over_root (radius 1),
fillet_wall_profile_smooth_at_root (0.8), fillet_wall_profile_corner_at_root
(1.2) and fillet_wall_profile_corner_sharp_end (1.6).

